    "contentMarkdown": "### I. Vocabulary & Pronunciation Mastery\n1. **Thematic Vocabulary for My New School**:\n* Key words and phrases commonly used in this unit:\n  - *Definition and meaning*: Vocabulary: school things, subjects. Grammar: Present Simple.\n  - *Word forms*: Noun (Danh từ), Verb (Động từ), Adjective (Tính từ), Adverb (Trạng từ).\n  - *Collocations*: Common combinations with verbs like *do, play, have, take, go*.\n\n2. **Pronunciation Guide**:\n* Practice distinguishing target sound contrasts (e.g. /s/ vs /z/, /t/ vs /d/, short vs long vowels).\n* Stress patterns in two-syllable and three-syllable words.\n\n---\n\n### II. Core Grammar Summary & Structure Table\n| Grammar Point | Structure / Formula | Example Sentence | Usage Note |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Affirmative (+)** | S + V(s/es) / Ved / will V | *She studies English every morning.* | Check subject-verb agreement |\n| **Negative (-)** | S + do/does/did not + Vbare | *They don't go to school on Sundays.* | Always return verb to base form |\n| **Interrogative (?)** | Do/Does/Did + S + Vbare? | *Do you enjoy reading science books?* | Yes, I do. / No, I don't. |\n| **Special structure** | Dependent clause / Comparison | *This test is more challenging than that one.* | Use correct adjective form |\n\n---\n\n### III. Illustrative Step-by-Step Examples\n\n#### 📌 Example 1 (Vocabulary in Context):\n* **Context**: Choose the best word to complete the sentence about daily school life.\n* **Sentence**: *\"Students at My Hoa Lower Secondary School always _______ their homework before going to class.\"*\n* **Analysis**: The subject is \"Students\" (plural), frequency adverb \"always\", verb collocation with \"homework\" is **do** (not make).\n* **Correct form**: **do**.\n\n#### 📌 Example 2 (Sentence Transformation):\n* **Original Sentence**: *\"She likes collecting stamps in her free time.\"*\n* **Requirement**: Rewrite using the phrase **\"Her hobby is...\"**.\n* **Step-by-step Solution**:\n  - Identify the subject: \"Her hobby\".\n  - Followed by the linking verb \"is\" + Gerund phrase: \"collecting stamps\".\n* **Result**: **\"Her hobby is collecting stamps.\"**\n\n#### 📌 Example 3 (Guided Paragraph Writing):\n* **Topic**: Write a short paragraph (50-60 words) about your daily routine or favorite activity related to \"My New School\".\n* **Suggested Structure**:\n  - Topic sentence: *My favorite activity is...*\n  - Supporting sentences (reasons, frequency, with whom): *I usually... because it helps me...*\n  - Concluding sentence: *I really love it and hope to...*\n\n---\n\n### IV. Common Errors & Tips for Vietnamese Learners\n1. **Omitting \"-s/-es\" in 3rd person singular**: Remembering that he/she/it takes Vs/es in Present Simple tense.\n2. **Incorrect Preposition Usage**: Confusing *in, on, at* for time and places (*at 7:00 AM, on Monday, in June, in My Hoa*).\n3. **Translating directly from Vietnamese (Word-by-word translation)**: Avoiding sentences like *\"I very like English\"* (Correct: *\"I like English very much\"*).\n\n---\n\n### V. Mind Map & Practical English\n* **Unit Summary**:\n  - My New School\n    ├── 1. Thematic Vocabulary (15-20 active words)\n    ├── 2. Core Grammar Rule & Formula\n    ├── 3. Pronunciation & Intonation\n    └── 4. Real-life communication (Introducing yourself, school projects, English club discussions)\n* **Real-world Practice**: Practice speaking with your classmates in the  English Club every week!",
